1
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:13,140
Rohan-sensei!

2
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:14,477
Thanks for meeting up with me.

3
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:16,277
It's a beautiful day, isn't it?

4
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:18,595
What's that book you're reading there?

5
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:20,211
Uh, the Steel Collection.

6
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:21,877
Death Steel?

7
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:24,136
Is that a new rock band or something?

8
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:27,837
He was a Russian-born artist.

9
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:30,100
I believe he died in 1955.

10
00:00:32,180 --> 00:00:33,800
By the way, Kaigamori,

11
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:37,237
I know full well that in
the working world at large,

12
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:40,791
being late for any business
meeting is considered improper.

13
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:41,950
However,

14
00:00:42,033 --> 00:00:44,057
an editor arriving six minutes early for a

15
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:46,457
meeting with his manga
artist is equally rude,

16
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:47,481
don't you think?

17
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:50,360
Oh, I'm so sorry about that.

18
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:52,137
Arriving early is a bad thing, then?

19
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:54,297
You're lucky you're meeting with me.

20
00:00:54,380 --> 00:00:55,397
But on to business.

21
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:59,127
You want to talk about my upcoming
61-page one-shot manga, no?

22
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,817
Excuse me, Rohan-sensei.

23
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:01,997
We're huge friggin' fans!

24
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:03,417
Can we please get your autograph?

25
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:07,080
Can you make mine out to my
pal Akira? Cut it out! Mr.

26
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:09,062
Kishibe's not giving autographs.

27
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:11,457
Can you see he's hard at work?

28
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:12,677
He doesn't have time!

29
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:13,819
It's already done.

30
00:01:15,760 --> 00:01:18,407
Unlike some manga artists,
I'm a fast worker.

31
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:21,060
I always have time to thank my fans.

32
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:26,600
Two-trip-part autographs done in
coffee?! No way! Thank you, sir!

33
00:01:26,780 --> 00:01:27,837
We'll treasure these!

34
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:32,837
Actually, if you wouldn't mind?

35
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:34,597
There is something personal
I'd like to discuss.

36
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:36,257
before we get down to business.

37
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:37,170
Sure.

38
00:01:37,253 --> 00:01:39,717
To be perfectly frank,
it's a question about cash.

39
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,397
More specifically, my payment.

40
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:42,310
All right?

41
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:44,537
Could you pay me in advance?

42
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:46,561
I've actually just gone bankrupt.

43
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:47,730
What?

44
00:01:47,813 --> 00:01:49,697
I haven't gone into debt yet, but...

45
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:51,540
right now, I'm homeless.

46
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:56,947
I'm staying at Koichi's at the moment,
but I don't even have a desk to work on.

47
00:01:57,660 --> 00:02:02,189
My Sailor Moon figures, Led Zeppelin
paper jacket CDs, Rurouni Kenshin manga.

48
00:02:02,420 --> 00:02:03,437
I've sold them all.

49
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:04,540
Slow down a sec!

50
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:06,637
You don't have anywhere to work?

51
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:07,550
And bankrupt?

52
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:10,657
Didn't you just buy yourself an
entire mountain the other day,

53
00:02:10,740 --> 00:02:12,117
complete with vacation cottages?

54
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,157
I told you before,

55
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:15,017
I bought it to investigate
the rumors of the

56
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:17,317
monster that lives on
that hill for my manga.

57
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:20,637
But then I heard those developer bastards
wanted to build a resort up there.

58
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:25,417
So I bought the six surrounding hills to
put a stop to their sleazy little plan.

59
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:28,317
More land equaled more influence,
so what else was I to do?

60
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:30,812
I bought it all to stop the construction.

61
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:34,797
But with plans for the resort
canceled, the land's value plummeted.

62
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:37,717
Now that area's just wilderness
in the middle of nowhere.

63
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:41,094
The six hills I just bought
are basically all worthless.

64
00:02:41,580 --> 00:02:43,260
Which means I'm flat broke.

65
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:45,537
Do you think you could
offer me in advance?

66
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:47,400
Let me process all this.

67
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:52,017
Did you really buy all those hills
solely for manga research purposes?

68
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:52,930
Yeah.

69
00:02:53,013 --> 00:02:53,843
Not as an investment?

70
00:02:53,926 --> 00:02:54,756
That's correct.

71
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:56,537
I'm shooting for reality here.

72
00:02:56,620 --> 00:02:59,137
In your comic about a
folktale monster on a hill?

73
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:00,050
You heard me.

74
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:02,217
Imagine if they did build the resort.

75
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:04,577
All that traffic could have
scared the monster elsewhere.

76
00:03:04,660 --> 00:03:07,560
In which case, my plan
would be for naught.

77
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:11,940
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

78
00:03:12,140 --> 00:03:13,357
What's with that face?

79
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:14,797
Can't you look me in the eye?

80
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:16,460
Hey, you're looking away.

81
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:20,777
Hey, you think that I've gone
completely off my rocker, don't you, Mr.

82
00:03:20,860 --> 00:03:22,320
Editor? Listen up.

83
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:26,437
Souped-up supercars and basement video
game theaters are fine and dandy,

84
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:29,696
but they're not the only
things manga artists can buy.

85
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:31,470
Hmph.

86
00:03:31,553 --> 00:03:33,237
And what's more, I did find it in the end.

87
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:35,908
So you see, my research
was worth every yen.

88
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:37,760
Listen carefully,

89
00:03:37,980 --> 00:03:42,098
and don't tell anyone outside the
magazine what I'm about to tell you.

90
00:03:42,340 --> 00:03:44,737
You found it? What?

91
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:47,055
What exactly are you saying you found?

92
00:03:47,220 --> 00:03:48,100
Oh, come now.

93
00:03:48,340 --> 00:03:50,377
Do you not listen to
people when they talk?

94
00:03:50,460 --> 00:03:52,060
I saw it with my own eyes.

95
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:55,217
The monster of Mutsukabe Hill does exist.

96
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:58,100
And as of this moment,
it lives there still.

97
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:05,237
I hate to ask, Rohan-sensei, but
could you please say that again?

98
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:06,540
What lives there?

99
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:15,060
There was a girl named Naoko Osato, a
student in her last year of college.

100
00:04:15,420 --> 00:04:19,940
But as September came to a close,
she would murder her boyfriend.

101
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:38,440
Thank you.

102
00:05:12,540 --> 00:05:13,720
Naoko Osato,

103
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:16,355
the only daughter of the Osato family,

104
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:20,852
who found their fortune making Masa in
Mutskabe village for over 300 years.

105
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:28,197
The Osato estate stood at the end
of a single track road upon a hill,

106
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:31,500
which is to say, the The
entire hill was theirs.

107
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:44,620
Hey, could you go home for the day? Huh?

108
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:47,995
And clean up the game stuff, will you?

109
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:51,360
What's going on?

110
00:05:51,820 --> 00:05:54,237
Someone from the main
house coming to visit?

111
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:55,202
Does it matter?

112
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:57,304
You can leave through the back.

113
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:58,580
Come on, now.

114
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:04,369
Lately, you've been, I don't
know, kind of chilly toward me?

115
00:06:04,580 --> 00:06:07,580
I don't want to ask this,
but is there another guy?

116
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:12,982
You just spared me the
trouble of an explanation.

117
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,757
Look, I'm not going to deny that
we've had some good times together,

118
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:19,637
but it's not going to work out
as long as my dad's around.

119
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:21,367
You're a part-time gardener.

120
00:06:22,140 --> 00:06:25,877
And as my dad's only daughter, I'm
supposed to protect the family fortune.

121
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:26,790
We're done.

122
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,300
I Don't think so?

123
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:33,197
You don't mean that come on.

124
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:35,697
What's wrong with keeping our thing going?

125
00:06:35,780 --> 00:06:37,898
There's no reason for us to split up

126
00:06:38,620 --> 00:06:41,377
How do you think they would
react if they came in and saw

127
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:44,931
us like this your precious
father in this new man of yours?

128
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:47,280
Let me fucking go!

129
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:49,750
You...

130
00:06:49,833 --> 00:06:50,663
you bitch!

131
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:53,860
I'm sorry.

132
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:55,217
I didn't...

133
00:06:55,300 --> 00:06:57,300
after you hit me, I just reacted.

134
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,700
I really do love you now.

135
00:06:59,980 --> 00:07:03,877
I mean, even if we have to keep it
secret, I'm happy just the way things...

136
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:04,790
Go on!

137
00:07:04,873 --> 00:07:07,680
Get out of here! Please,
now. Listen... Go!

138
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,520
Take the damn money and go home already!

139
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:16,157
Well, we didn't exactly tell
her we were coming, did we?

140
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:17,946
She'll probably be flustered.

141
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:21,100
Bet she'll try to do
herself up in record time.

142
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:25,264
I'll be at the door any minute.

143
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:29,477
Gunpei, please take your
stuff and get out of here now.

144
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:32,913
To be perfectly honest, you're
the one I want to be with.

145
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:35,137
But this is the man I've been engaged to.

146
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:39,297
My family has decided that we'll be
getting married after I graduate college.

147
00:07:39,380 --> 00:07:40,837
So this is the end for us.

148
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:42,802
We can't see each other anymore.

149
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:53,210
Gunpei?

150
00:07:58,940 --> 00:07:59,770
Hey.

151
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:15,870
No.

152
00:08:15,953 --> 00:08:18,137
If this is another one of
your jokes, it's not funny.

153
00:08:18,220 --> 00:08:20,097
Another prank, right? Gunpei.

154
00:08:20,180 --> 00:08:21,597
Stop playing around.

155
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:24,717
I don't feel a pulse. He's...

156
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:25,920
He's dead.

157
00:08:29,380 --> 00:08:34,697
Not knowing what else to do, Naoko Osato
decided to dress Gunpei's wound regardless.

158
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:38,140
She pressed a towel she found
nearby against his head.

159
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:40,820
This has to be some kind of trick.

160
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:42,260
It can't be true.

161
00:08:42,580 --> 00:08:44,360
I just gave him a little push.

162
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:50,620
Why was that golf club there?

163
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,110
Why?

164
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:54,197
This makes it look like...

165
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:55,640
Like I...

166
00:08:56,240 --> 00:09:00,177
This makes it look like I took the
golf club and beat him to death!

167
00:09:00,260 --> 00:09:01,090
Gunpei.

168
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:03,340
What should I do?

169
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:04,720
A doctor.

170
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:06,440
I'll call a doctor.

171
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:11,616
But if he's dead already,
I'll let doctor be any help.

172
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:15,760
Oh god, do I have to
call the cops instead?

173
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:19,660
Naoko, are you in there?

174
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,080
It's me, dad.

175
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:23,960
And I brought Shuichi along with me.

176
00:09:24,220 --> 00:09:26,140
He's sure excited to see you.

177
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:33,960
No, I'm not here.

178
00:09:35,660 --> 00:09:37,460
I'm not anywhere at all.

179
00:09:40,460 --> 00:09:42,700
Huh. It's locked. Hmm.

180
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:45,041
Maybe Naoko isn't here after all.

181
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:48,900
It may have been my imagination, Mr.

182
00:09:49,040 --> 00:09:53,040
Osato, but I could have sworn I saw
that window screen move earlier.

183
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:08,840
I need to do something with his body.

184
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:19,097
What's going on he
doesn't have a pulse his

185
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:22,004
heart's not beating so
why is he still bleeding?

186
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,640
Naoko, are you there?

187
00:10:26,140 --> 00:10:27,200
What's going on?

188
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:28,560
Are you alright?

189
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:30,595
I've got a spare key.

190
00:10:30,860 --> 00:10:32,036
Let's open the door.

191
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:33,230
Oh, father!

192
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:34,820
I didn't hear you.

193
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:37,613
You caught me tidying up in the kitchen.

194
00:10:38,060 --> 00:10:39,980
Ah, so you are home.

195
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:42,720
Guess who's here. Shuichi.

196
00:10:43,780 --> 00:10:44,610
Really?

197
00:10:44,740 --> 00:10:45,740
How wonderful.

198
00:10:46,460 --> 00:10:48,877
Could you ask him to wait
for me in the main house?

199
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:51,017
Naoko, your voice sounds a little off.

200
00:10:51,100 --> 00:10:54,440
Are you alright? Do you
need a hand? No, I'm okay.

201
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:56,337
Just changing into something nicer.

202
00:10:56,420 --> 00:10:58,185
So please don't open the door.

203
00:10:58,380 --> 00:11:00,615
I'll be with you in a minute, promise.

204
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:04,767
Please don't open that door!

205
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:33,088
What the hell is happening?

206
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:38,085
How is it even possible for humans to keep
bleeding like this after they're dead?

207
00:11:40,660 --> 00:11:43,131
Naoko, you're using an awful lot of water.

208
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:44,418
What are you up to?

209
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:46,640
It's me, Shuichi.

210
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:50,597
I bet you're wondering what
I'm still doing out front here.

211
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:52,800
Honestly, it was your father's idea.

212
00:11:53,180 --> 00:11:57,709
He lent me the spare key so you and I
could spend more quality time together.

213
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:00,120
No! Damn!

214
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:02,461
You can't come in no matter what!

215
00:12:04,580 --> 00:12:06,700
Naoko, I actually saw someone.

216
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:10,456
A figure in the window as I
was approaching the house.

217
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:13,887
It looked like someone
was in there with you.

218
00:12:14,420 --> 00:12:16,057
Are you alone in there right now?

219
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:21,800
Well, I could have sworn that I saw
one other person in the house with you.

220
00:12:24,060 --> 00:12:24,980
I'm sorry.

221
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:26,200
I'm sorry.

222
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:28,400
But this is all your fault anyway.

223
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:30,580
I didn't do anything wrong.

224
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:51,111
Naoko, are you all right?

225
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:55,240
So there is someone else in there.

226
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:57,820
Gunpei, please!

227
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:01,220
Stop bleeding, you have to stop!

228
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:06,939
That's it, I'm coming in right now!

229
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:39,440
You mentioned you saw
someone else in here with me?

230
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:41,621
Who might that have been, Suichi?

231
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:47,930
Please...

232
00:13:48,013 --> 00:13:50,197
Please stop...

233
00:13:50,280 --> 00:13:52,257
Please stop...

234
00:13:52,340 --> 00:13:54,220
Unpei... I'm sorry...

235
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:58,830
Stop.

236
00:13:58,913 --> 00:14:00,080
Please forgive me.

237
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:06,217
Hey, I'm really sorry about that.

238
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:08,476
Talk about an overactive imagination.

239
00:14:08,860 --> 00:14:12,507
I'll go join your father in the
main house until you're ready.

240
00:14:20,220 --> 00:14:22,080
And so, as arranged,

241
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:27,344
Naoko was married the next spring, and
Shuichi was welcomed into the Osato family.

242
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:35,100
But ever since that day, Gunpei Kamafsa
has never once stopped bleeding.

243
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:40,300
Every day, he quietly
bleeds about 300 cc's.

244
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:44,148
If his body is not moved, he
will never bleed more than that.

245
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,860
However, the bleeding is continuous.

246
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:53,511
Despite the fact that any and all signs
of life have completely disappeared.

247
00:14:55,640 --> 00:15:00,160
Naoko Osato has never once been on a
trip away from home since her marriage.

248
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:02,740
And every morning...

249
00:15:03,980 --> 00:15:09,060
She takes a glass bottle full of Gunpei's
blood and discreetly discards it.

250
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:10,480
A daily ritual.

251
00:15:11,180 --> 00:15:16,200
She does this without fail so as to hide
it from the prying eyes of her family.

252
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,320
Hey Naoko, come and eat with us.

253
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,280
I'll be right there.

254
00:15:29,960 --> 00:15:33,877
Ever since the detached guest house
was demolished for conversion.

255
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:37,117
Hidden in the attic above
the closet in the main house.

256
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:39,080
Lies Gunpei.

257
00:15:42,220 --> 00:15:44,420
